From 7ac620a1133a4d1566dc7ea0799c86df9b727764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Zheng <bluevisor@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:08:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Appearance: color themes with light and dark variants,
 picture buttons

Replace the "Dark mode" check box in Colors with two picture buttons, Light and Dark, and add six themes as picture buttons (Haiku, Ocean, Forest, Graphite, Sunset, Lavender). Each theme has a light and a dark variant: a window tab color, an accent (progress bars, selections, check marks, keyboard focus) and a hue mixed into the background colors, on top of the built-in light or dark color set. Haiku is the built-in sets unchanged. The selected theme and variant are recognized from the current colors, so nothing new is stored; custom colors select no theme. Choosing Light or Dark keeps the theme.
